  "acceptance_id": "pocky_syringe_two_cycle_v1",
  "notes": "Headless two-cycle syringe dispense PASS/FAIL: dispense packet 1, the operator pulls it out, then dispense packet 2. Cycle 1 events packet_exit and packet_presentation and checks exactly_one_packet and pickup_ready are copied from syringe_dispense3_acceptance.json (pocky_syringe_dispense3_v1), every number unchanged; that file takes them from the frozen acceptance.toml (raw SHA256 518a45ffc4592ca602be4c33c59681038e43dedaa15b688312202c3a57ff6ca2) with its own recorded identity and support bindings, and takes the housing thresholds and penetration/validity from s0_acceptance.json (raw SHA256 150c037b2e985dac46b66670c46291872d9e0cc9d287d7946eadf4d9185b5a3a). Binding changes in this file versus the frozen documents, and the only ones: (1) Inherited from dispense3: packet_exit and packet_presentation bodies are [packet, packet_02, packet_03]; packet_presentation support_bodies is [housing] instead of [lip, body]; the S0 body/chassis pose and drop checks are bound to housing against floor_world with the S0 thresholds; the S0 contact_duration checks against pusher, rod and crank are omitted because those bodies do not exist; no settled-speed checks. (2) Cycle 2 repeats both events and both checks with names suffixed _2 (packet_exit_2, packet_presentation_2, exactly_one_packet_2, pickup_ready_2), every number identical to the frozen values, windows actuate_2 to hold_2, release_phase release_2, dwell release_2 to hold_2. The cycle 2 bodies are [packet_02, packet_03] only: packet 1 has been removed by the hand, is beyond the exit, and must not count as a second packet. This narrows the identity list for cycle 2 only because packet 1 is deliberately gone; packet_03 stays declared so an undeclared escape is still not a pass. (3) New check slider_home_release (return_displacement on slider_x at the end of release, reference 0, max 1 mm) proves the spring has returned the slider home before the operator waits and picks the packet up; return_displacement reads the joint position at the end of the named phase, which is the right generic kind for an absolute home position (joint_displacement measures a difference between two phases). (4) Housing pose and signed world-z drop checks (S0 thresholds, window max_over_phase, drop measured from initial) are repeated for actuate, press_hold, release, hold, actuate_2, press_hold_2, release_2 and hold_2. They are deliberately not applied during pickup, pickup_hold or settle_2, because the hand pulling the packet may tug the housing. Honest limitation on dwell: the frozen dwell_min_s is 0.5 s and is unchanged. In this scenario the dwell window is release plus hold, 0.5 s + 0.25 s = 0.75 s, and the operator waits only 0.25 s after release ends; the packet must therefore be stable from the start of release, not only after the slider has returned (it is expected home within about 0.1 to 0.3 s). The same applies to cycle 2, whose hold_2 is 1.5 s and release_2 is 0.5 s. The pickup phases apply a 3 N +X body force on packet only (ramped over the pickup phase, then constant) and are outside every event window. No settled-speed checks are carried over. Expected outcome is not asserted before the run.",
